  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. It replaces a record naming the owner as reviewer, because that record's fingerprint no longer matched; that record stays in git history. Read http_profile.signature_base_composition and http_profile.wire_surface_closure. sigbase.rs: resolve_component_value now picks an Origin (request or response) from the source message and the req flag, refusing when a response-only source is asked for a ;req component or a request source is asked for one (the old code refused the same two cases), then resolves the derived component (method, target-uri, authority and path from a request origin; status from a response origin) or a field. field_value finds the one case-insensitive header match, refuses none or a second, and trims spaces and tabs; this is the old loop. signature_base evaluates each component in order before serialising the parameters, as before. sf_dictionary.rs: split_dictionary and split_parameters share split_top_level over a QuoteScan that treats a backslash inside quotes as escaping one character and splits only outside quotes; labelled_value keeps the empty-member refusal, the neighbour-prefix skip and the label-without-value refusal in the same order. signature_parameters.rs: check_tail_spelling refuses when the tail is non-empty and does not start with a semicolon, has an empty segment, or has a space or tab outside quotes, with the same error. The tests only moved behind request_base_error and assert_refused, and the RequestSignature argument. The claim holds. The mutation lane was not run, and no test was run. Evidence class as registered (V0).",
